# Provisioned by argus into each task worktree under .worktrees/<name>.
# Grammar: one `copy <pattern>` or `symlink <pattern>` per line, pattern
# relative to the repo root (docs/worktree.md §5.4).
#
# All three are symlinks rather than copies: they're either shared state we
# want edits to propagate through (.env) or too heavy to duplicate per task
# (node_modules, .venv). A pattern that matches nothing is only a warning,
# so a fresh clone without a .env still creates worktrees fine.
#
# Re-apply to worktrees that already exist: argus worktree apply <name>

symlink  .env
symlink  node_modules
symlink  .venv
